 orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+7\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-\\sqrt{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{1}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e43d27-ffaf-58ea-bb6e-664b70770003" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Orthogonal Basis For the Span of Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5656b367-1c88-55a1-875c-750e7807eaf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365789} {:answer/id #uuid "2cea23b0-05a2-51b2-9f96-61763e7d4f7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365790} {:answer/id #uuid "9b2d3e9e-3259-518b-9f66-b9f6e9b2f5fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365791} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3cb2c9-5125-5e9a-904f-9e92e79f0f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365792} {:answer/id #uuid "e5401aca-16af-53f6-8306-f53bb2e714e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :a