v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot 1}{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $b=5,$ $c=-2,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{-2}{5}=-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e43d27-ffaf-58ea-bb6e-664b70770003" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Orthogonal Basis For the Span of Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a82679fe-6639-5fca-9f72-7474315e71b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365817} {:answer/id #uuid "51e2a39e-37e2-5c74-b5af-6ef521b99da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365818} {:answer/id #uuid "c63d7a57-579c-5fd2-84f4-a68233800a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365819} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbc748-18ad-523f-a667-28b08fe93713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365820} {:answer/id #uuid "0e53b82c-a368-5464-86d7-fc9d4f99bb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e53b82c-a368-5464-86d7-fc9d